#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5fa7b5b-ee3b-5ec5-82f7-0d5489952a88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533661}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533661} :answer-field/id #uuid "0993d2df-afb2-5918-abc9-0085f57ccea0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f04b7aa7-21c0-58cb-a044-6cd8f614ccdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533729}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533729} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b2f56de-5698-580f-a95c-fdc0907069d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df1c126c-4286-537f-a872-e032f4f131ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533690}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533690} :answer-field/id #uuid "f07a1f18-7d90-5690-825e-3d3440849512" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "def3b7cd-4317-5941-a403-30fe46331281" :question/math-academy-id "q-269498" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"3\" width=\"8px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"45px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"45px\">$0$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"3\" width=\"8px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\">$-32$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{3}.$ Then, $L(A)={y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}({y}^{T}y)=2y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}=2{y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is $2$ times the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=2y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =2y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =2(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =2(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2(\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -32 & -32 \\\\ 16 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccc7cd39-2b31-5e60-9f7f-6d6dbdd6fcd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4280" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533633}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533633} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a1b8af5-7b32-59e0-af44-041131fdb958" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "847371f3-c4cc-51af-87c4-80f81681286d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "480" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533450}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533450} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b35ca60-322b-555a-a5bd-d55c7f80941e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533897} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4b7f285-21bd-5c63-961f-8c698aa411e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4280" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533702}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533702} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8bb2f47-6b22-5ef2-a095-870537c2a058" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fe59fe2-e68f-5e11-84b7-67ac73d71ee2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "480" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533360}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533360} :answer-field/id #uuid "f55e12fe-6e05-5d4a-be95-d4e0ff57c8bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e1b5136b-802c-5748-926e-3ce486df5870" :question/math-academy-id "q-269472" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=(2Ax-b)^{T}(2Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$-240$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2140$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=2Ax-b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)={y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}({y}^{T}y)=2y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}=2{y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=2Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}=2{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=2{x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}\\cdot 2{x}_{j} \\\\  & =4{y}_{i}{x}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n The $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is $4$ times the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=4y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\n Finally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =4y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4(2Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4(2\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =4(\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 110\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}48 \\\\ 428\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}480 & 480 & -240 \\\\ 4280 & 4280 & -2140\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57509c8b-6b98-51aa-9762-9963caf04358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536435} {:answer/id #uuid "581f54a2-60c9-5dc5-bb4d-f8f318fe2d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536440} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4429f4-c191-50e8-be52-084fe635f47b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536488} {:answer/id #uuid "bfecac8a-fa87-5d62-a946-7f122c1e66c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536585} {:answer/id #uuid "f1218c8e-974e-52d6-b624-68fd43f78159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536667}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536585} :answer-field/id #uuid "b518b34a-8d6e-54eb-93d9-d3cb5a0505b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6a4bb009-1382-5d80-b122-5cf6749f1552" :question/math-academy-id "q-138615" :question/problem "$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e278261-12a2-522a-865f-2ee4f991690d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536414} {:answer/id #uuid "95c87fe0-b27d-523b-b97f-283a3892f373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536522} {:answer/id #uuid "ad6e45b4-0d19-5a65-9da0-878c4f37d052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536562} {:answer/id #uuid "c24f6fe3-8f3b-5e4f-87ee-cd603ef7bb00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536590} {:answer/id #uuid "c4625cbc-5b19-59bd-9eb5-2085cc809466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536595}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536562} :answer-field/id #uuid "9980a067-163c-5305-b9d5-aeb44a51e2ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-138608" :question/problem "$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f060f18-5f38-57d0-8035-ee521e1efa10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536447} {:answer/id #uuid "63f36174-881c-57cb-888e-5b635ad28017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536456} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9c88b3-2c09-54a3-99c5-91c575160cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536463} {:answer/id #uuid "82ed669f-a9bd-5e1c-8760-9d608342f7c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 42\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536499} {:answer/id #uuid "e3398816-b77b-5ead-950a-9a70459413a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536639}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536447} :answer-field/id #uuid "63610fdd-4a0f-5e58-8e91-40c9b79c1b2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d39bfe0e-e6e3-509a-9ccb-2651e206d7a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-138639" :question/problem "$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nSo, we first need to compute the mean-deviation form of our observation matrix.\n\nThe sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample covariance matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{3-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e5a2d37-c4d6-5c27-bc7b-4ea71231b6a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537359} {:answer/id #uuid "46d8d0ee-ed43-5b82-b677-585c48864035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537376} {:answer/id #uuid "94896345-dcbf-5311-af2f-0470b2af33bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537507} {:answer/id #uuid "b31e0d65-4eac-54bf-b80e-d663776fb997" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537575} {:answer/id #uuid "b91ee488-df0e-59db-a257-d1dabeda41e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537588}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537376} :answer-field/id #uuid "9313c766-b074-562e-915b-c0a2bae81c97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3a6241f6-827e-5f45-a2f2-3047ca1b82e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-86769" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⇒\\,{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-48 \\\\ 17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{38}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 18\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-48 \\\\ 17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537968 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fad72e3-bee7-5eb3-9828-6bf06dfaa7af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537256} {:answer/id #uuid "b435f2e3-4cd8-585d-954c-52f87c1f4746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537577} {:answer/id #uuid "cb246cd3-9bbb-53e2-b543-1ad93f9bd8ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537626} {:answer/id #uuid "f69ae65b-9be7-53cf-91f1-13dc37eb2f46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537735} {:answer/id #uuid "fb15ad4b-aa77-523c-bd0d-f2171314bac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537747}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537626} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e225e4-0bfc-5b26-8ce8-66c5aba780de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cc66ebbe-2cca-5407-87bc-772df677089f" :question/math-academy-id "q-86762" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {(\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {\\begin{bmatrix}17 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 17\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263e9c79-2b5d-5fc6-ae10-bec804651dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}30 \\\\ 42\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539553} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6bef22-fee1-53f1-8d0f-2529ad295f2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}30 & 42\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539639} {:answer/id #uuid "85ee42d0-6b46-5068-8546-0b6d45122f68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539700} {:answer/id #uuid "a2df55cc-4d93-55a0-9838-4a5a0b419174" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}58 & 26\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539752} {:answer/id #uuid "ae374fd7-8d71-5715-bb99-e0fa0ee5417f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}58 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539776}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539776} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ae1559-7267-51e9-bbdf-d599082e8f60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3f634cb0-d91f-55a0-8036-9bf4e6795f5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-269525" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=(Ax-2b)^{T}(Ax-2b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=Ax-2b.$ Then, $L(x)={y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{T}={\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{T}\\cdot {\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y}\\right)}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{T}y)=2{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(Ax-2b)=A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{T}\\cdot {\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y}\\right)}^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =2\\cdot {A}^{T}(Ax-2b) \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}(\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}(\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}58 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed298814-70d0-5656-b6e2-258ce3641ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-992" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541924}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541924} :answer-field/id #uuid "00abc28b-95f9-5105-a5d2-782d2db3d65a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7d3c641-98ec-536a-b7ca-05afeccd2ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541915}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541915} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fefe5d8-100f-5282-b59e-0d1be2e84a1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "43f1cf78-e476-5744-a4e1-4eb640602151" :question/math-academy-id "q-269517" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=(4Ax-5b)^{T}(4Ax-5b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$832$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=4Ax-5b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)={y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}({y}^{T}y)=2y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}=2{y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=4Ax-5b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}=4{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-5{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=4{x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}\\cdot 4{x}_{j} \\\\  & =8{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is $8$ times the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=8y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =8y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =8(4Ax-5b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =8(4\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =8(\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}208 \\\\ -248\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 832 \\\\ 0 & -992\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e1e29d1-1888-52aa-8dc6-4b2845f73611" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541611} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fa668de-a737-5f91-800a-6c4b031f88c5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542015} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33107365-8d72-59e7-84e4-fb7248465cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541529} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd131918-eda5-51aa-9124-e861cbcfd218" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a276eb8e-dc20-5069-8231-5e2d2d2a281a" :question/math-academy-id "q-269429" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}(\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y)=y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}={y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 \\\\ -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "976542d7-dd7f-5daf-aab6-bb5f2d5588dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541737} {:answer/id #uuid "9c769625-2afb-52e2-9006-b7df92b8cd0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541748} {:answer/id #uuid "a54b3b29-5e7b-5355-993d-c1692b182224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541763} {:answer/id #uuid "af1b5240-994c-562c-9dae-36bc16150a71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541781} {:answer/id #uuid "cf9d05e7-08ac-5c52-8f0b-08fb9cac8514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541862}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541748} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6e05b4e-adf0-5ec5-b639-9d019a4a9d63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ae4e117c-08e3-5ee2-be97-840ec47e6061" :question/math-academy-id "q-269381" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=2({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 10 \\\\ -5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=2(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=2(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0\\end{bmatrix})=2(\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2237675a-cbb8-55f4-ac1e-48c201dc4645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545270} {:answer/id #uuid "b366e033-8b4f-533d-86e0-d5b107bc8270" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545525} {:answer/id #uuid "d71b0cc6-29c4-5b34-b310-64ab60f5b724" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545592} {:answer/id #uuid "d90fb75f-16a5-5779-817f-22c451b4191b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545597} {:answer/id #uuid "fe29b5e6-ad57-590e-8812-0f23650c5a45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545668}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545592} :answer-field/id #uuid "a810a855-c6d2-5045-a468-45c2987823ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5e7c8be1-d271-506d-bfc9-fbf1881a88d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-142489" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle \\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =5 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f1b4ae3-0a40-5756-bb35-332f91366150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545226} {:answer/id #uuid "341ea572-fea0-5ab5-8e97-94b9de3afc39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545303} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc8c0b7-7f8f-5ba1-a69b-9e3d9da97a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545318} {:answer/id #uuid "73232096-0842-59cd-811b-a3783597953d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545416} {:answer/id #uuid "855804bf-27d3-5391-ba94-a4c1ff073b30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545452}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545226} :answer-field/id #uuid "c143e0e6-92b8-5ab3-a31a-0f6f3f8892c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c10d4c77-93c5-52a9-900d-275fa9299d3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-79410" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{4}$\n\nIII. $A$ has $2$ pivot colums" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since the non-zero vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nspans $\\text{Null}(A),$ we conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=1.$ So, by the rank-nullity theorem, with $n=4$,  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=\\text{rank}(A)=3,$ we must have  that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The fact that $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=3$ implies that the number of pivot columns in $A$ is also equal to $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549018 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1456d1-c217-5333-894e-c3d90b3be143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548406} {:answer/id #uuid "754b876d-1c1d-5fa2-8c8a-19930e540b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548569} {:answer/id #uuid "e516614c-5556-5ad9-a091-72667d82e048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548801} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ce0150-7f6b-597d-9302-bb72b972307e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548843} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b099a0-b60b-53de-9964-15d50b6188cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548849}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548849} :answer-field/id #uuid "3112cc9b-c99d-5760-8709-44ca37572265" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7b9e6797-8ad6-50af-aa3b-75e9f9aa6e0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96689" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 11 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Which of the following is a basis of the eigenspace corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =7?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =7.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 11 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 5\\end{bmatrix}-7\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required basis is\n\n$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed71b383-87bf-5f68-ada3-9d1bf1621ac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549190} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d08e6d2-9a18-5194-a4b5-165cf4314c1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ad1cffd-57ce-5a4f-a1cd-b9fbff93cc2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549158} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b5ea60-f49d-4454-b3ca-33a25b151406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567256}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549158} :answer-field/id #uuid "116f97d9-f00b-5591-922a-1ef0fdecd620" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549161} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea7088cb-ea64-581e-9d0c-06c86aa2806f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549188}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549188} :answer-field/id #uuid "59444d8a-71d5-5b63-ac16-5bf6f0124a5a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6314a6-7119-5799-b95a-c3c20df968e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549160} {:answer/id #uuid "f8147fbe-e7a7-440f-b51d-f9cb82bb85a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567257}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549160} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fe0afe9-1d61-57c1-ad29-7092d170f3d8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6d7739fd-3f62-54a0-8f08-2be277540be7" :question/problem "Calculate $A-(B-C)$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$A-(B-C)=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(B-C) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}9-0 & -1-0 \\\\ 0-0 & 7-(-9)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9-9 & -9-(-1) \\\\ -1-0 & -7-16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -23\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6067054-7fd7-5494-afbc-63d2f1559965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549192}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549192} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b02cda3-58fa-5c92-bb86-7f7f1f78a064" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549164} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "999ac731-f8fe-5bbb-ae2e-9746750317db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549180}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549180} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c8db2d3-ed99-542c-a1d7-a2a23d3ad80f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1f35416-70b6-5829-b9cd-2cd827d01541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549184}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549184} :answer-field/id #uuid "ead897d3-b824-5616-bcee-21308edbe47a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a251c7a8-7766-5b09-be0f-9d9cdd3ec615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549182}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549182} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee94a05b-d8df-5eec-bd5a-b787df804ab2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9c991876-ebda-5ae9-97e2-83fe985af8de" :question/problem "Calculate $A+(B-C)$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ -7 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$A+(B-C)=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+(B-C) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}+(\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ -7 & -4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-9-3 & -1-6 \\\\ 8-(-7) & 6-(-4)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & -7 \\\\ 15 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+(-12) & 8+(-7) \\\\ 1+15 & -4+10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 1 \\\\ 16 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d78a2e84-a85a-5426-839b-d919d6d4b21d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549187}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549187} :answer-field/id #uuid "3962cc30-d68b-50e2-9773-d6aedf315071" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549163} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3791a3cb-3358-5c4f-9a27-646be33d615b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549162}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549162} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d46fe0e-797a-5fd0-bf21-fd0f6cbd02ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f9923ef-6fcf-5a18-8db6-2620b208228a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549175}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549175} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a9c1505-e38c-556b-8560-5c2cc406c445" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d2eef1e-ff06-5df1-8eb1-4ea4bf0598df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549171} {:answer/id #uuid "a11b4970-75f7-48a8-b344-592b1d637ccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567254}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549171} :answer-field/id #uuid "95636e19-16b7-5501-af4d-c1cea649ce07" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d25c4306-6441-5c4f-87fe-15896c66e824" :question/problem "Calculate $C-(D-E)$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$D=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -9 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$C-(D-E)=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C-(D-E) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -9 & -2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4-(-2) & 6-0 \\\\ 7-(-9) & 5-(-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 16 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2-6 & -4-6 \\\\ 8-16 & -1-7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -10 \\\\ -8 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4d4fb6a-d27b-55cc-8727-67a4c04b568b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "760" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549652}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549652} :answer-field/id #uuid "86a09f03-3f8a-5c3f-9183-dbfb9af6dd2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eeb1139b-d9f2-55ff-8169-1877c0fc480b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549755} :answer-field/id #uuid "a107a0f3-3d37-50c0-a77a-33925b86f16a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "078844cb-65ac-54f4-bde7-64e4bd44f313" :question/math-academy-id "q-269466" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=2(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$760$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-40$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)=2{y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}(2{y}^{T}y)=4y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}=4{y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i}.\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =4{y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =4{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is $4$ times the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x,$ so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=4y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =4y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =4(\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}76 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}760 & 760 \\\\ -40 & -40\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "298e07ae-5f8c-52b7-8fdb-05f8ff2eb333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 28 & -14 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549407} {:answer/id #uuid "3b2813e9-da8e-59ae-9d0e-61e685a4f322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549437} {:answer/id #uuid "a2aefe95-7159-51aa-88da-37aecf1ef5f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 28 \\\\ -14 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549626} {:answer/id #uuid "af6ac5dd-6929-5011-8bf3-a504e287864a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 14 & -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549644} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a8f364-5251-5618-b38b-b49e3fc2960c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549407} :answer-field/id #uuid "8abf474a-1fab-5810-988c-58859ca7b121" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7c674592-16b0-5e5a-b0ac-ce1e62f430e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-269369" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=2({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}2{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=2{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=2(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=2(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix})=2(\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 14 & -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 28 & -14 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551286 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32904df2-4f2b-512e-b905-4f4eebcb813e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550488} {:answer/id #uuid "b50b8760-3a6d-55c4-a188-c37cf457dc61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550863} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fc2b8c-e26a-5dd7-a42a-b9a4b347b89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550998} {:answer/id #uuid "f98c45d9-1ef2-58e4-b974-3eb63756e062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551036} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcf0b97-a0e4-515d-9606-6b57bb04f711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551057}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550863} :answer-field/id #uuid "f732bcd0-c8c8-5638-93ed-8a183c2c0d4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6ad7a8de-9677-5fd6-a871-171f20886f2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130788" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $N$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[N\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12} & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:=12{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 12\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{N}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d2b6588-f32d-5385-bd36-7b8f041a190c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550480} {:answer/id #uuid "683fbbc1-c806-50d9-85a2-308dfd7a7a36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550627} {:answer/id #uuid "75aa5e5b-700c-53ad-aec6-1adbaed46b85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550663} {:answer/id #uuid "a76d076d-96cf-5f10-aa9f-cad8b99ef4fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550663} :answer-field/id #uuid "13b526db-cf02-5f36-a044-7d6b75922f0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "591b2b7e-b01c-5e07-a746-ed180d35a0a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550586} {:answer/id #uuid "aa586531-3bcc-503b-820e-4330f043b12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550823} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa0ff68-b962-565a-bfdd-c76ff445cc7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550825} {: